Aerie-Purpose: Name the Linux desktop entry, app ID, icon, user data directory and audio client Aerie, so the desktop shows Aerie and no Helium data directory is reused.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/common/channel_info_posix.cc, chrome/common/chrome_paths_linux.cc, chrome/browser/shell_integration_linux.cc, media/audio/pulse/pulse_util.cc, chrome/installer/linux/common/chromium-browser.info
Aerie-Kind: branding

The desktop entry is aerie.desktop and the icon theme name is aerie (both
files are in packaging/linux). The app ID (reverse-DNS name, used as the
metainfo id and the installer RDN) is io.github.pedrosousa13.aerie. The user
data directory is ~/.config/aerie. The HELIUM_DESKTOP and HELIUM_CONFIG_HOME
environment variables keep their names: they are not shown to users.

